## Start here

- People: this file, then the [documentation map](docs/README.md).
- AI agents: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). `CLAUDE.md` imports it for Claude Code.
- Setting up the code: run `/afe-init` in Claude Code. It asks the owner what to build and with
  which stack, records the answers, scaffolds the code, and wires the checks into this template.

## Checks

```bash
scripts/check.sh
```

Requires Git, bash, and Node.js 20 or later; nothing else to install. External links are not
checked; a project that wants it adds a check such as [lychee](https://lychee.cli.rs/) in
`scripts/checks.d/` (`docs/documentation-rules.md`, section 9).

## Protected main branch

Changes reach `main` only through pull requests with passing checks, merged with a merge
commit. After the first push, a repository admin applies the repository settings and the GitHub
ruleset once (`--dry-run` shows them first): merge commits only and "Automatically delete head
branches", on every plan; secret scanning with push protection, which a private repository may
need GitHub Advanced Security for; and a ruleset on `main` that requires a pull request, allows
no deletion or force push, and requires the checks `check` and `integrity`{% if fail_without_change %} (and, once
set as below, `base`){% endif %}, and only these.
Rulesets need a public repository or, for a private one, a paid plan.

```bash
scripts/protect-branch.sh
```
{%- if fail_without_change %}

Once the `base` job of the `fail-without-change` workflow passes in CI on a pull request that
changes a test, not as a SKIP, run it again with `--require-base` to require that job too; the
label `tests-pass-on-base` still lets a test that passes on the base through.
{%- endif %}

## Project template

This repository is generated from
[`create-afe-project`]({{ template_url }}); `.afe-answers.json` records the
template version. The template owns the files listed in `.template/owned.sha256`; change them
in the template and update this repository with `npx create-afe-project@latest update`
(`docs/contributing.md`, section 5).
